# The diamond tour: a 450 mm square driven at 45 deg to the start
# heading, so its legs run diagonally across the field rather than
# along its axes.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. square.tour used to LOOK like this on the chart, and
# that was an artifact of plotting in the robot's inherited odometry
# frame rather than anything the robot drove (see square.tour's own
# header). Charts render in the start frame now, so square.tour draws a
# square. This file is the figure that was being asked for: a diamond
# ON PURPOSE, produced by a 45 deg entry pivot.
#
# It is not just square.tour rotated for looks. A square exercises the
# drivetrain along one axis at a time; a diamond puts every leg at 45
# deg to the field, which is the orientation a staging or geofence
# error is most likely to show up in, and it is the harder figure to
# fit -- the diagonal of the square becomes the bounding box.
#
# SIZING. A square of side S turned 45 deg spans S*sqrt2 in BOTH axes.
# With the working budget of +-550 x +-350 mm (tours/FIELD.md), the
# tight axis gives S*sqrt2 <= 700, so S <= 495. 450 mm sides span
# 636 x 636 mm and leave ~32 mm on y. Stage the robot at the WEST
# vertex -- the figure runs 0..900 mm in y and +-450 mm in x from the
# start point -- so start at (0, -450) relative to the field centre.
#
# The entry pivot is NOT undone at the end: the tour closes on the
# diamond, and the robot finishes on the 45 deg heading it started
# driving on. A trailing -45 deg pivot would return the original
# heading but would also add a fifth rotation to a figure whose whole
# point is four.

# PIVOT TUNING (MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01, interleaved A/B so battery
# drift hits both arms equally). Pivot cruise 188 mm/s (omega 180 deg/s)
# beats 300 mm/s (286 deg/s) decisively: excess +1.34 deg sd 0.35 versus
# +6.88 deg sd 1.03, n=8 each. pivot_overrun was then swept AT 188 mm/s
# and 0.68 -- the value the closure sweep found at 300 mm/s -- leaves
# +1.44 deg on the table; 2.0 is the zero crossing (1.8 -> +0.29,
# 2.2 -> -0.25). pivot_overrun is speed-dependent: retune it whenever
# the pivot cruise changes.

SET twist_hold_gain 8
SET speed_floor 512
SET yaw_taper 800
SET pivot_overrun 2.0

# --- enter the diamond: turn 45 deg off the start heading ------------
MARK entry
TWIST omega=180 angle=45 timeout=6

MARK leg1
TWIST vx=250 dist=450 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=250 dist=450 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg3
TWIST vx=250 dist=450 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=250 dist=450 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.5
